  "scientific_conclusion": "The lightweight spatial saliency prototype (TinySalNet) trained under DHF1K saliency-density supervision demonstrates substantial predictive capability beyond the trivial uniform baseline across all primary saliency metrics (NSS, AUC-Judd, KL divergence, CC, SIM). Saliency metrics measure 2D spatial density alignment and are fundamentally distinct from 1D scalar fixation-concentration proxy metrics (MAE/R^2). In accordance with Phase 7 protocol, this model remains a research prototype and is not integrated into production."
